---
import DesignSystemLayout from '../../layouts/DesignSystemLayout.astro';
---

<DesignSystemLayout
  title="Compound Health Design System"
  section="Overview"
  lede="The single source of truth for what the marketing site looks like and how it behaves. Built using atomic design and the Finsweet Client-First naming framework. This area is internal and noindexed."
>

  <section class="ds-section">
    <div class="ds-section-head">
      <h2>How this system is organised</h2>
      <span class="ds-tag">atomic + client-first</span>
    </div>
    <p class="ds-note">
      Atoms are the smallest visual primitives: a colour, a type style, a button, an input. Molecules
      combine atoms into reusable patterns: a credibility item, a step card, a form field. Organisms,
      templates, and pages are out of scope for v1 — they are assembled directly inside
      <code class="ds-inline">src/pages/*.astro</code> using molecules and global section classes.
    </p>
    <p class="ds-note">
      Tokens live as CSS custom properties at the top of <code class="ds-inline">src/styles/global.css</code>.
      Class names follow Client-First conventions: lowercase, hyphen-separated,
      <code class="ds-inline">component-element</code> structure for variants, and
      <code class="ds-inline">is-active</code> / <code class="ds-inline">is-open</code> for state.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="ds-section">
    <div class="ds-section-head">
      <h2>Sections</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="ds-overview-grid">
      <a class="ds-overview-card" href="/design-system/atoms">
        <span class="ds-overview-card-eyebrow">01 · Atoms</span>
        <h2>Atoms</h2>
        <p>
          Colour, typography, spacing, radii, buttons, badges, eyebrows, dots, dividers,
          form inputs, avatars and icons. Everything that cannot usefully be broken down further.
        </p>
        <span class="ds-overview-card-meta">/design-system/atoms</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ds-overview-card" href="/design-system/molecules">
        <span class="ds-overview-card-eyebrow">02 · Molecules</span>
        <h2>Molecules</h2>
        <p>
          Step card, plan card, testimonial, credibility item, metric row, post card, author chip,
          tag chip, form field, mobile menu link. Atoms combined into reusable building blocks.
        </p>
        <span class="ds-overview-card-meta">/design-system/molecules</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ds-section">
    <div class="ds-section-head">
      <h2>Working rules</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="ds-note">
      One: every visual change starts here. If a token, atom, or molecule does not exist for what you
      need, add it before using it. Two: do not inline colours or sizes on elements. If a value is
      reused, it lives in <code class="ds-inline">global.css</code> as a token or class. Three: this
      directory and everything under it must stay noindexed and out of
      <code class="ds-inline">public/sitemap.xml</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

</DesignSystemLayout>
